 "about_text": "Craft Contemporary is a nonprofit museum in Los Angeles dedicated to contemporary art made from craft media and processes. It traces its roots to The Egg and the Eye, a restaurant-gallery opened in 1965 by painter Edith Robinson Wyle, which gained nonprofit museum status in 1973 as the Craft & Folk Art Museum. Renamed Craft Contemporary in 2018, the institution presents exhibitions by established and emerging artists and designers often underrepresented in larger art institutions, paired with hands-on workshops and public programs. Located on Wilshire Boulevard's Museum Row, it continues a decades-long tradition of using craft to engage Los Angeles communities through exhibitions, festivals, and educational initiatives.",
